38:30&nbsp;

00:38:30.310 --> 00:38:39.520
Cristine: Yes, for sure. I’m going to tell you&nbsp;
about my whole journey with meditation. I did my&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:38:39.520 --> 00:38:50.080
yoga, got that down, and then I knew I was meant&nbsp;
to explore Eastern meditation. My first glimpse at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:38:50.080 --> 00:39:02.720
that was actually a movie called Doing Time, Doing&nbsp;
Vipassana. Real meditation looked like Vipassana&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:39:02.720 --> 00:39:13.040
to me. That requires ten days of silence. There is&nbsp;
a Vipassana retreat within distance from me that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:39:13.040 --> 00:39:21.600
I could have done, but I was like, “I don’t&nbsp;
know how I’d do that.” In the documentary it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:39:21.600 --> 00:39:30.160
shows how Vipassana changed the nature of one&nbsp;
of the worst prisons in the world in India.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:39:40.080 --> 00:39:49.920
They brought it into the prison and it transformed&nbsp;
the inmates — reduced the general issues, created&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:39:49.920 --> 00:39:54.800
better dynamics with the guards. It was really&nbsp;
transformative. I thought that was so interesting.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:39:56.720 --> 00:40:08.320
I did a teaching about principles around Eastern&nbsp;
meditation on 11/11/11 at 11 a.m. I’m all about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:40:08.320 --> 00:40:21.680
the numbers. November 11, 2011, I opened this&nbsp;
door in a big way. I went on record saying,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:40:21.680 --> 00:40:28.480
“I hope I do not have to go to prison to&nbsp;
learn how to meditate.” It felt like a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:40:28.480 --> 00:40:36.720
prison concept to me. I couldn’t imagine ten days&nbsp;
of silence unless there was nothing else to do.&nbsp;

00:40:40.480 --> 00:40:47.520
Later I encountered a former Buddhist monk&nbsp;
who sat with me. I hadn’t been able to get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:40:47.520 --> 00:40:57.120
into silence and stillness, so he worked with me.&nbsp;
He taught me Mahasati, which is a movement-based&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:40:57.120 --> 00:41:14.080
meditation — like a transition between yoga&nbsp;
and meditation. Then we started talking about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:41:14.080 --> 00:41:25.120
my deepest fears. I had this fear that if I&nbsp;
were completely silent and still, it wasn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:41:25.120 --> 00:41:36.800
safe. I associated it with non-existence. My&nbsp;
deepest fear was that I would cease to exist,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:41:36.800 --> 00:41:42.800
and the more still and silent I was, the more I&nbsp;
felt like I fell into that fear. The doings and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:41:42.800 --> 00:41:49.360
the act of motion was like a survival mechanism&nbsp;
for me. My subconscious felt like I was alive and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:41:49.360 --> 00:41:57.840
I existed as long as I was doing. Being wasn’t&nbsp;
as safe, because at some level — and it has to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:41:57.840 --> 00:42:05.120
do with that emptiness in me — it was like I would&nbsp;
fall into the black hole of nothingness. I worked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:05.120 --> 00:42:15.040
with him on that fear for a while, and through&nbsp;
that I was able to grasp zero. When we talk about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:15.040 --> 00:42:22.880
that neutrality, there is something beyond that&nbsp;
on a quantum level that is actually the zero point&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:22.880 --> 00:42:30.720
field, where all energy is removed from a system.&nbsp;
It is actually a ceasing of all. This thing that I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:30.720 --> 00:42:38.080
was so afraid of, I actually had to move through&nbsp;
it. In moving through it I found — and some of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:38.080 --> 00:42:44.400
this was through quantum entrainment; Dr. Frank&nbsp;
Kinslow is an advocate of this pure awareness — he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:44.400 --> 00:42:53.360
talks about this transition from the zero point&nbsp;
field to the unified field. There’s an amazing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:53.360 --> 00:43:01.280
teacher of Transcendental Meditation that also&nbsp;
talks about this: John Hagelin. John Hagelin is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:01.280 --> 00:43:07.520
a quantum physicist who’s also a Transcendental&nbsp;
Meditation teacher. He talks about the same kind&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:07.520 --> 00:43:23.520
of thing. There’s the dense 3D stuff, like a&nbsp;
chair. Underneath that you’ve got molecular&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:23.520 --> 00:43:34.720
composition, then atomic, then subatomic,&nbsp;
particles, the quantum weight… and when all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:34.720 --> 00:43:42.000
of that’s gone, you’ve got the zero point field.&nbsp;
But adjacent to the nothing is the everything,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:42.000 --> 00:43:52.560
the all. In Buddhism that’s also a principle — the&nbsp;
empty bowl, the Zen. If you take everything out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:52.560 --> 00:44:07.520
including ego, you have the potential for all, the&nbsp;
vastness of Source to enter. I started to get this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:07.520 --> 00:44:21.280
and recognize that that black hole fear was really&nbsp;
just a tunnel to the everything, or a transition&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:21.280 --> 00:44:33.520
place. I actually created a technique, a&nbsp;
meditation practice based on all this information,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:36.720 --> 00:44:49.920
called Quantum Wholeness Meditation. Then I went&nbsp;
to do TM. There’s a teacher here in Salt Lake. He&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:49.920 --> 00:44:56.880
mentioned that there are more billionaires than TM&nbsp;
teachers, and I thought, isn’t that interesting?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:58.880 --> 00:45:11.040
There’s only one in Utah. I felt really privileged&nbsp;
to have that experience and learn about Maharishi&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:45:11.040 --> 00:45:25.680
Mahesh Yogi. I still am very much a fan. That&nbsp;
led me to other solutions. I stuck with the 20&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:45:25.680 --> 00:45:35.520
minutes twice a day for months, and then went back&nbsp;
to Quantum Wholeness Meditation, partly because I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:45:35.520 --> 00:45:41.360
do better and am more committed to it as a group&nbsp;
practice. I’m one of those people that I’m going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:45:41.360 --> 00:45:45.920
to do yoga if I go to yoga class and there’s other&nbsp;
people in the room and somebody’s guiding me. I do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:45:45.920 --> 00:45:52.880
meditation if I know it’s Monday at 12:30 and&nbsp;
we’re studying A Course in Miracles and doing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:45:52.880 --> 00:45:56.240
meditation with intention together.
45:55&nbsp;

00:46:00.880 --> 00:46:17.120
Jacob: That’s so cool that you had all that&nbsp;
